# Supplier Portal core

Before domain work, load the matching project skill(s) under `.cursor/skills/` and read the docs they cite. Do not duplicate skill bodies here.

| Work | Skill |
|------|--------|
| Architecture, stages, business rules | `supplier-portal-architecture` |
| Prisma, Neon, migrations, quantity/reserve invariants | `prisma-neon-safety` |
| Auth0, guards, supplier isolation, permissions | `auth-supplier-isolation` |
| Implementation, tests, lint/typecheck/build, stage QA | `feature-dev-qa` |
| UI, brand, mobile, a11y, motion, performance | `ui-ux-performance` |

## Permanent product principle

**Supplier does the minimum. Company handles the complexity.**

Supplier-facing UX must stay simple (few clicks/fields, mobile-first, one obvious next action, plain language). Company users own receipt verification and GRN. Details live in `ui-ux-performance` and `supplier-portal-architecture`.

## Global gates (pointers only)

- Confirmed Stage 5B/6A + implemented delivery/receipt rules live in docs + `supplier-portal-architecture` — preserve them.
- Unresolved decisions: ask; never invent.
- Neon development only; no production writes without authorization; no destructive DB resets; migrations require explicit approval (`prisma-neon-safety`).
- Supplier isolation and authz enforced in application code (`auth-supplier-isolation`).
- Prefer existing server actions and domain queries; never silently change business behavior during UI work (`feature-dev-qa`).
- Do not edit root `AGENTS.md` (Next.js-maintained). Use it only for Next.js version guidance.
